  "correctAnswer": "B",
  "explanation": "Choice B is correct. First, find $g(2)$: $g(2) = 2(2)^2 + 5 = 2(4) + 5 = 8 + 5 = 13$. Then find $f(g(2)) = f(13) = 3(13) - 7 = 39 - 7 = 32$. Next, find $f(2)$: $f(2) = 3(2) - 7 = 6 - 7 = -1$. Then find $g(f(2)) = g(-1) = 2(-1)^2 + 5 = 2(1) + 5 = 2 + 5 = 7$. Finally, calculate $f(g(2)) - g(f(2)) = 32 - 7 = 25$.",
